        SKELETON, deliberately. The shared Java wrapper surface - the API both transports
        implement and the nine other languages mirror - lands with the Java reference
        implementation on the language-proxy plan (astubbs#242). Seeded empty so the module tree,
        aggregator entries and data fragments exist before any code does. Transport types (gRPC,
        protobuf) must never appear on this surface; the direct sibling's dependency ban is what
        makes that checkable.
